.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt URTSX 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm urtsx
.Nd Realtek USB SD card host controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "urtsx* at uhub?"
.Cd "sdmmc* at urtsx?"
.Cd "ld* at sdmmc?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Realtek RTS5129 USB card reader with vendor ID 0x0bda
and product ID 0x0129.
It connects the controller to the
.Xr sdmmc 4
subsystem, which discovers the card and provides block devices through
.Xr ld 4 .
.Pp
The initial implementation supports SD memory cards at 3.3 volts,
with one data line and a maximum clock of 25 MHz.
It transfers one block at a time through the controller's 512-byte buffer.
Card detection uses a cached status value.
USB requests run in process context.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
This implementation supports read access only.
It rejects data writes, erase commands, lock commands and persistent switches.
The reported write-protect switch state remains the physical card state.
.Pp
SDIO, MMC, UHS, 1.8-volt signalling and multiblock transfers are not supported.
Memory Stick and xD media are not supported.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ld 4 ,
.Xr rtsx 4 ,
.Xr sdmmc 4 ,
.Xr usb 4
